---
// The shape of every DNS message, question or answer: a 12-byte header and four sections. The
// same format travels over UDP, TCP, DoT and DoH.
---

<svg viewBox="0 0 400 392" width="100%" role="img" aria-labelledby="dns-msg-t dns-msg-d">
  <title id="dns-msg-t">Inside a DNS message</title>
  <desc id="dns-msg-d">
    A stack of five parts. The header, 12 bytes: an ID that matches the answer to the question,
    flags such as QR (this is an answer), AA (authoritative), TC (truncated) and RD (recursion
    desired), a result code such as NOERROR or NXDOMAIN, and a count for each section. Then the
    question: a name and a type. Then the answer section with records, the authority section with
    NS or SOA records, and the additional section with glue and the EDNS OPT record that says how
    big a UDP answer the sender can take. A note at the bottom: over UDP, if the answer does not
    fit, the server sends the header with TC set and the client asks again over TCP.
  </desc>

  <g font-size="19">
    <rect x="4" y="4" width="392" height="96" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-flow-soft); stroke: var(--viz-flow)" />
    <text x="16" y="30" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Header, 12 bytes</text>
    <text x="16" y="56" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">ID 0x3f2a  QR AA TC RD RA</text>
    <text x="16" y="84" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">RCODE NOERROR  counts 1/1/0/1</text>

    <rect x="4" y="108" width="392" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-client-soft); stroke: var(--viz-client)" />
    <text x="16" y="132" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Question</text>
    <text x="16" y="154" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">api.shop.example.test. A</text>

    <rect x="4" y="172" width="392" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-ok-soft); stroke: var(--viz-ok)" />
    <text x="16" y="196" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Answer</text>
    <text x="16" y="218" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-ink); font-family: var(--sl-font-mono)">api… A 203.0.113.10 TTL 2</text>

    <rect x="4" y="236" width="392" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="16" y="260" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Authority</text>
    <text x="16" y="282" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">NS for referrals, SOA for "no"</text>

    <rect x="4" y="300" width="392" height="56" rx="6" stroke-width="2" style="fill: var(--viz-server-soft); stroke: var(--viz-server)" />
    <text x="16" y="324" font-weight="700" style="fill: var(--viz-ink)">Additional</text>
    <text x="16" y="346" font-size="17" style="fill: var(--viz-muted)">glue; OPT: "I take 1232 bytes"</text>

    <text x="200" y="384" text-anchor="middle" font-size="17" font-weight="600" style="fill: var(--viz-warn)">too big for UDP → TC=1 → ask over TCP</text>
  </g>
</svg>
